  "question": {
    "text": "Let S be the set of all the words that can be formed by arranging all the letters of the word GARDEN. From the set S, one word is selected at random. The probability that the selected word will NOT have vowels in alphabetical order is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "e78FG",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "x0eTM",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vYV8z",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DF3wV",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "A, E,G R D N\n$\\text { Probabllity }(\\mathrm{P})=\\frac{\\text { favourable case }}{\\text { Total case }}$\n(when A & E are in order)\nTotal case $=6$ !\nFavourable case $={ }^6 \\mathrm{C}_2 .4$ !\n$P=\\frac{(15) 4!}{(30) 4!}$\n\nProbablity when not in order $=1-\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$",
    "image": null
